The first DLC for Crimson Desert hits in October. - Game Informer
Crimson Desert: Charting The Unknown DLC Introduces Underwater Diving, Naval Combat, And More Next Month
Crimson Desert launched in March, and since then, developer Pearl Abyss has been hard at work removing generative AI art , improving the game's story with narrative patches , adding cross-save support , and releasing an "Enhanced Version" last month . Now, the studio is ready to release its first DLC. Titled "Charting The Unknown," this DLC adds plenty of maritime activities to protagonist Kliff's massive adventure, and it arrives on PlayStation 5, Xbox Series X/S, and PC on October 15.&nbsp;
The trailer for Charting The Unknown, which was featured in today's PlayStation State of Play , showcased Kliff exploring the ocean alongside what appears to be a shark companion, captaining a ship in a very Assassin's Creed Black Flag Resynced style, creating a beachside house using the game's base-building mechanics, and more. Plus, this DLC will continue Kliff's story after the base game's ending, and he will encounter new bosses and discover new weapons, armor kits, and more.&nbsp;
Check it out for yourself in the Crimson Desert: Charting The Unknown DLC trailer below:&nbsp;
"Reclaim power and reach beyond – into the unknown," the DLC's description reads. "The story of Pywel continues in Crimson Desert: Charting The Unknown as Kliff, Oongka, and Damiane set out to discover their purpose and shape their futures. However, as turmoil unfolds around them, each must fight to forge a path through the trials ahead. Join them on a new adventure and discover what new possibilities await across Pywel."
Crimson Desert: Charting The Unknown launches on PlayStation 5, Xbox Series X/S, and PC on October 15.&nbsp;
In the meantime, read Game Informer's Crimson Desert review .&nbsp;
What do you hope to see in this DLC? Let us know in the comments below!

LEGO has partnered with Sony for yet another console throwback build. - Game Informer
LEGO PlayStation Design Revealed
Today’s State of Play revealed a new partnership between the brick-building toy makers at LEGO and the PlayStation brand. Following on the heels of other video game console models like the NES , Game Boy , and Sega Genesis , the new LEGO PlayStation looks like a nostalgic throwback focused on celebrating the origins of the original 1994 design.&nbsp;
The LEGO PlayStation includes several features and gimmicks that should bring a smile to the face of gamers who recall that mid-'90s console. The set includes both an opening button, a light, and a controller that can be plugged into the larger set. Borrowing the idea from other successful brick-built recreation sets, the LEGO PlayStation also includes two hidden dioramas that nod to early successes for the PlayStation brand – one focused on Ape Escape and the other on Gran Turismo.&nbsp;
As of the State of Play airing, LEGO hadn’t revealed too much more. However, in a subsequent posting to the LEGO official site , we learned that the piece feature 1911 pieces, is set to release on October 4, and will retail for $179.99. &nbsp;
